trace.content:
[THOUGHT] All eight evidence domains have now been systematically addressed:  
1) Chief complaint & onset — fatigue (months), bumps (3 weeks, left thigh);  
2) Course — fatigue predates bumps, no progression or triggers reported;  
3) Associated symptoms — no weight loss, night sweats, or itch; appetite/sleep unknown but not volunteered;  
4) Past medical history — denied chronic illness;  
5) Medications & allergies — none reported;  
6) Social/occupational/exposure — repeatedly unable to recall specific exposures, including skin-to-skin contact;  
7) Physical exam — three 2–3 mm, dome-shaped, hardened, umbilicated papules confirmed;  
8) Lab/imaging — CBC normal; ACE, CXR, biopsy, and dermoscopy all unavailable or not specified.  

No further diagnostic yield can be obtained within the 16-turn limit. The clinical picture is most consistent with molluscum contagiosum — the classic umbilicated papules — though the prolonged fatigue remains unexplained and may be coincidental or require separate evaluation. All domains are complete.

[FINISH]

